TASK-186.2 runtime harness: dev mode's toolbar above the page, per pane, with
navigation, the copy and URL controls, the docked Web Inspector on every
side, the per-site switch, a Peek, the find bar, light and dark, and a second
window's snapshot. Temporary code, never committed to Detour/. Apply, build,
run, revert:

    git apply docs/harness/task186-2-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    xcodebuild -scheme Detour -configuration Debug build -derivedDataPath .derived
    # $SITE/app.html and $SITE/remote.html: a <title>, an <h1>, a coloured top
    # border and a line printing innerWidth x innerHeight (updated on resize):
    python3 -m http.server 8862 --bind 127.0.0.1 --directory "$SITE" &
    DETOUR_DATA_DIR=DetourVerify1862 DETOUR_VERIFY_DIR="$OUT" DETOUR_VERIFY_PORT=8862 \
        .derived/Build/Products/Debug/Detour.app/Contents/MacOS/Detour &
    # a watcher reads only the new lines of $OUT/verify.log every 0.2 s and
    # runs `screencapture -x -o -l <windowNumber> $OUT/<name>.png` for each
    # "SHOOT <name> <windowNumber>" line; the harness waits for each PNG
    # before its next step. Wait for "done" (about 100 s), then kill that
    # pid and the server.
    git apply -R docs/harness/task186-2-harness.patch && xcodegen generate
    rm -r -- ~/Library/Application\ Support/DetourVerify1862

The local site is localhost:8862; the remote one kubernetes.docker.internal:8862
(127.0.0.1 in /etc/hosts, not local by the rule). The inspector is driven with
`webView._inspector` `show` and `attach` (it attaches at the bottom by
default), then `InspectorFrontendHost.requestSetDockSide('bottom'|'right'|'left')`
evaluated in the inspector's own web view (the container's other
WKWebView, a WKInspectorWKWebView). WebKit saves the side in the SHARED
com.detourbrowser.mac defaults as
`__WebInspectorPageGroupLevel1__.WebKit2InspectorAttachmentSide`: the run
docks back to the bottom, and the key (absent before) was deleted afterwards.
The shell-launched app is not active, so window 2 takes the web view over
through `windowDidBecomeKey` called directly. The copy step saves and restores
the general pasteboard.

Results (2026-10-24, second run after the corner fix; all 25 captures read
and matching the log; container 972x760):
