First run found the page of a re-hosted split pane rounded at the TOP
(corner mask chosen by `contentsAreFlipped()`, which read unflipped while
the pane was re-hosted); fixed to decide from `isFlipped`.
Not driven: window fullscreen, element fullscreen, a person's real mouse
drag on the toolbar background (moves the window via performDrag).

